      "content": "To pinpoint the cause of the unexpected temperature spike, initiate a thorough inspection of the reefer unit. Start by checking the refrigeration cycle logs to identify any anomalies or errors coinciding with the incident. Examine the ice build-up levels, evaporator fan functionality, and compressor operation for signs of mechanical distress.\n\n\nEnsure the thermal insulation is intact and has no visible damage. If sensors and digital controls were tampered with or malfunctioned, conduct a system-wide audit to track any unauthorized adjustments or errors. Investigate the power supply continuity to the unit both in transit and upon arrival to ensure stable electrical input.\n\n\nInspect the ambient temperature surrounding the reefer during transit, as changes could impact the cooling efficiency. Analyze transport route data for any delays or deviations from the planned path that may have caused prolonged periods in extreme temperatures and correlate this with the technical documents of the containment unit for a complete investigation.",
